  "title": "What Secure Attachment Really Means",
  "content": "Secure attachment is the deep sense a child has that their caregiver is emotionally available, responsive, and safe. It is not about being perfect or constantly cheerful. It is about being consistent enough that a child trusts you will return, listen, and care. Children with secure attachment explore more confidently, recover from stress more quickly, and form healthier relationships throughout life.\n\nMany parents worry that they have already damaged attachment, but attachment is flexible and repairable. Even if a parent has made mistakes, secure attachment can still form through repeated moments of connection, comfort, and responsiveness. What matters most is the pattern over time, not isolated moments.\n\nThis lesson helps parents understand the foundations of secure attachment and why it is one of the strongest predictors of a child’s emotional wellbeing.",
  "activities": [
    "Spend five minutes today giving your child your full attention—no phone, no distractions. Notice how they respond.",
